-- title:
--   Change of avoided set for localised Hecke algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$, let $S_0 \subseteq S$ be sets of natural numbers, and for a set $S$ write $\mathbb{T}^S =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$; since $S_0 \subseteq S$ there are fewer generators for $S$, so [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra_mono`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L45) gives $\mathbb{T}^{S} \le \mathbb{T}^{S_0}$, with associated inclusion map. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete (adically complete for its maximal ideal) discrete valuation domain with residue field $k$. Assume that the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the lattice spanned over $\mathbb{Z}$ by the weight-two cusp forms of level $N$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are integers is the whole space. Let $\theta_0 : \mathbb{T}^{S_0} \to k$ and $\theta : \mathbb{T}^{S} \to k$ be ring homomorphisms such that $\theta$ is the restriction of $\theta_0$ along the above inclusion. Then there is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\Psi :$ `heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ` $\to$ `heckeLocal N S₀ 𝒪 θ₀` between the corresponding localised Hecke algebras (each being the localisation of `heckeBaseAlgebra` at the image under `latticeBaseChange` of the complement of the prime `heckeCharKernel` attached to the relevant character) which is a local homomorphism and satisfies $\Psi(\pi(t)) = \pi_0(t)$ for every $t \in \mathbb{T}^{S}$, where $\pi$, $\pi_0$ are the structure maps [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.π`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L151) and $t$ on the right is viewed in $\mathbb{T}^{S_0}$.
--
--   This is the elementary comparison map between the localisation of a Hecke algebra generated by fewer operators (for instance an anemic algebra, where $S$ contains the primes dividing $N$) and the localisation of the algebra generated by more operators at a maximal ideal refining the given one; it is in general neither injective nor surjective. It is used throughout the level- and set-changing manipulations of localised Hecke algebras, for example in the comparison of auxiliary levels and in the identification of $U$-eigenvalues at ramified primes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_heckeLocal_exists_algHom_of_subset.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeLocal

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algHom_of_subset
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (S S₀ : Set ℕ) (hS : S₀ ⊆ S)
    (𝒪 : Type) [CommRing 𝒪] [IsDomain 𝒪] [IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) 𝒪]
    [Fact (CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2)]
    (θ₀ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀ →+* IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪)
    (θ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S →+* IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪)
    (hθ : ∀ t : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S,
      θ t = θ₀ (Subalgebra.inclusion (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra_mono hS) t)) :
    ∃ Ψ : CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ →ₐ[𝒪] CuspForm.heckeLocal N S₀ 𝒪 θ₀,
      IsLocalHom (Ψ : CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ →+* CuspForm.heckeLocal N S₀ 𝒪 θ₀) ∧
      ∀ t : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S,
        Ψ (CuspForm.heckeLocal.π N S 𝒪 θ t) =
          CuspForm.heckeLocal.π N S₀ 𝒪 θ₀ (Subalgebra.inclusion (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra_mono hS) t) := by sorry
